    * Phase-space (Tremaine-Gunn class): m >~ 0.3-1 keV (dwarf phase space) -- the framework's m passes trivially.
    * N_eff (the 2026 combined bound): Delta N_eff < 0.107 (95%): LBT Y_p + Planck + ACT + SPT + DESI (arXiv 2603.13226); Planck+BAO 2018: N_eff = 2.99 +- 0.17. See Part 3c.
    * Direct detection at keV masses: recoil searches (SENSEI/DAMIC-M/CRESST) do NOT reach a 5-keV fermionic WDM (recoil energy on electrons ~ 2.5e-5 eV -- sub-eV, below every ionization threshold); absorption-style searches (hidden photon / ALP at 5.09 keV: DAMIC, XENON) bound the EM coupling of an ABSORBING species -- not the WDM fermion.
  EVERY literature number above is CITED/UNVERIFIED -- the framework verifies none of it; it is the honest context the neighborhood owes.

