--- 3a. the radiative-decay line: E = m/2 ------------------------------
  IF the particle decays radiatively (X -> nu/gamma + gamma, massless daughter): E_gamma = m/2.
  E_line(m = 5.089) = 2.5443 keV  -- the 2.55-keV class
  canonical band: [2.5000, 2.5948] keV;  1-sigma band: [2.4958, 2.5927] keV;  G163 window: [2.30, 2.53] keV
  THE OBSERVABLE: a monoenergetic X-ray line at 2.55 keV (2.5-2.6 keV band) from DM halos (Milky Way, clusters, LMC/SMC) -- in band for XRISM/eROSITA/XMM and future Athena X-IFU.
  THE DECAY-RATE LIMIT, STATED HONESTLY: the framework fixes m but contains NO coupling or mixing angle: it does NOT predict the rate, the branching, or even whether the decay exists.  For orientation only (UNVERIFIED literature): a sterile-neutrino analog would give Gamma ~ (7.2e29 s)^-1 (sin^2 2theta/1e-8)(m/keV)^5, i.e. at m = 5.09:
      Gamma(sin^2 2theta = 1e-8) = 4.739e-27 s^-1  ->  lifetime 6.69e+09 Gyr;  at sin^2 2theta = 1e-11: 6.69e+12 Gyr (the line, if present, is cosmologically long-lived)
      -- a keV sterile's lifetime ~ 1e17-1e18 yr is why the line is so faint; the framework itself is silent on all of it.
      -- illustrative only; the framework itself is silent on all of it.
  [PASS] C9 [the line energy] E = m/2 = 2.545 keV, fiducial band [2.50, 2.60] keV
         measured: E_line = 2.5443 keV

