--- 3c. N_eff / T_0 consequences IF the sector is thermal at decoupling -
  A species decoupling relativistic at the neutrino temperature adds Delta N_eff = g_s/2 per 2-helicity fermion:
    Majorana-like (g_s/2 = 1): Delta N_eff = 1.00  ->  excluded at 14 sigma (N_eff = 2.990 +- 0.070, 2026 combined, UNVERIFIED; Planck 2018: 2.99 +- 0.17)
    Dirac-like (g_s/2 = 2):   Delta N_eff = 2.00  ->  excluded many sigma
  temperature needed to pass at 95%: T_s,dec < 0.572 T_nu (Delta N_eff = r^4 x g_s/2 <= 0.107).
  BUT the committed lambda_fs = 0.558 Mpc integral ASSUMES T_s,0 = T_nu,0 (r = 1): the relic face's own normalization is excluded by N_eff unless the sector decoupled colder -- which would shrink lambda_fs and contradict the committed 0.558 Mpc register.  HONEST TENSION: thermal-free-streaming and the committed N_eff-consistent geometry do not coexist.
  THE CDM-CONSISTENT FACE (G156/H047: R(k) = 1 at every k, no free streaming -- the COMMITTED ontology):
    non-relativistic decoupling: T_dec <= m/3 = 1.696 keV (T_dec ~ 1.97e+07 K) <-> z_dec <= 7.22e+06; the sector's radiation density is Boltzmann-suppressed: Delta N_eff ~ 0; T_s,0 ~ 3.77e-07 K -> v_0 ~ 41.5 m/s -> NO free streaming, NO N_eff, NO CMB distortion.
    T_0 consequence: a cold sector contributes nothing to T_0 / N_eff; its observable residue is (i) the 2.55-keV line (if EM decay), (ii) the phase-boundary temperature T_b = 9.17-9.52 K = T_CMB(z*), (iii) the 1e5-1e8 M_sun subhalo decade (G156 C8).
  [PASS] C11 [N_eff] a fully-thermal r = 1 decoupling is excluded by current N_eff (Delta N_eff < 0.107 at 95%); the committed CDM face (R = 1) is the non-relativistic-decoupling branch and carries no N_eff cost
         measured: Delta N_eff(r=1) = 1.00 vs 95% bound 0.107; cold branch T_s,0 = 3.8e-07 K

